{"title":"Topicwise Test-23 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EC Electromagnetics-2","fileName":"082_Topicwise Test-23 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EC Electromagnetics-2.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>An electromagnetic wave is propagated in an air-filled waveguide. If the phase velocity of wave inside waveguide is 5 × 10<sup>8</sup> m/s, then the angle of wave with the waveguide axis is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 30°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 53°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 60°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 37°</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/75af09b77a2e7444097f3dcc5b866f9525af26ce.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A circular waveguide has an inner diameter of X = 6 cm and the guide contains an air dielectric.<br />\nIf the the cutoff wavelength of guide is <em>Y</em> cm, then |<em>X</em>| + |<em>Y</em>| is<br />\n(Assume dominant mode propagation)</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 6 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 16.38 cm</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 12.32 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 10.38 cm</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e14ed4d8b827a52c7fe659f6b2c1f8108ec6a007.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A rectangular air filled waveguide carries TM<sub>11</sub> mode whose electric field in axial direction is given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\