smiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> tesla, then the value of <em>A</em> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/88a16ff8a9c04b522ffa92bbeeb70e33b8ff6305.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 10</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/46dafba0778df4e1b9b0ec12c6bba2047466fb18.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/387c5a682cb7d0e2cc7c1c76af292d2d84ef8498.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/85b95f3450ea13c225501696b501ad82c49844bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A copper wire has conductivity σ = 5.8 × 10<sup>7</sup> S/m, μ<sub>r</sub> = 1 and ∈<sub>r</sub> = 1, then the skin resistance of the wire at 50 MHz is ________ mΩ.</p>\n<p>(Rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.84","high":"1.84"},"solution":"<p>1.84 (1.50 - 2.00)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bf2e8868955a12eb6099bf134d39fe686b1635cb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a certain region for which σ = 0, μ = 2μ<sub>0</sub> and ∈ = 10 ∈<sub>0</sub>, the current density is <img src=\"/media/a0ef364cb259e2a9db78e39284ce066967e38b6d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> If the value of propagation constant, β = 15 rad/m, then the value of ω is _________ ×10<sup>9</sup> rad/sec.<br />\n(Rounded off to three decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1","high":"1"},"solution":"<p>1.000 (0.900 - 1.200)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8ec4615cfbc332679c841369636fe1884537f0d7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If the complex permittivity of a certain medium is 2–<em>j</em>, then the loss tangent of the medium is ____.<br />\n(Rounded off to one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.5","high":"0.5"},"solution":"<p>0.5 (0.4 - 0.6)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/87cc8f04adebe56ad82bbca1a14ec784637429da.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following is/are not the advantages of circular waveguides over rectangular waveguides?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Occupy less space for dominant mode</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Easy to manufacture</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Easy to join</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Changes plane of polarization for dominant mode.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, d)<br />\n&bull; The circular waveguide is easy to manufacture and join.<br />\n&bull; However, the cross-section of a circular waveguide is larger than that of a rectangular<br />\nwaveguide for carrying the same signal and thus, occupy more space.<br />\n&bull; The dominant mode (TE<sub>11</sub>) in a circular waveguide can experience rotation of its plane of polarization.<br />\nThus, statements (a) and (d) are not the advantages of circular waveguide.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The plane wave <img src=\"/media/9b179dc5deb92fb25a5b0b1acd28197680cb0ee8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> in air normally hits a lossless medium (μ = μ<sub>0</sub>, ∈ = 4∈<sub>0</sub>) at z = 0. The reflected magnetic field is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6315a012e4808f2d4b6d41947fb78d1b369042b1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/535f70e569c096f5dc7150d98a56e18b7d97d563.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/aeb103452da97aee84e29db413877a1ed03fec08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/d4a21b5e6a962e71e38fb9a1510c02319b096bb5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dd3bd46f1996f7af56458142fc505087f9e78d8e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1c748ec6dbce77d390daad0c270011ff84c93770.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>An EM wave travels in free space with the electric field component <img src=\"/media/94a9fc5b1f4d793743d22469b2bbf83a97918aee.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The time average Poynting vector of the wave is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/39b0d27fc00294211679aabf5f468ee965cff386.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/510eed8d0276b35f98ac82e2667166c50e4db816.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/49048c6d9a2b08b3b07549634a85f756e0a2a22c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/15ef70ce0ae2ff63345e33d7fa5616df381f7844.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b0ce13a1107de256c8b836f7e56a1ceb79ab53e3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A standard air filled rectangular waveguide has dimensions such that a = 2.2b. If the cutoff frequency for TE<sub>02</sub> mode is 15 GHz, then the phase constant for TE<sub>10 </sub>mode at 7.2 GHz is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 49.78 rad/m</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/824d6e9ea82b3e17f2245769489b327f35735818.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a5c250e380b1099d70336c68ac566a09682a1a12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 132.8 rad/m</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3ea1050af2cde2caf7b5af3dcc5d558ef227a304.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider an electric field phasor of a uniform plane wave travelling downward in water given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/cdbd7a60b5e2fee394645b93adffacb81b4c55c4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>where <img src=\"/media/237fbc73dd997627460d8a6c560594002eebb17d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is the downward direction and z = 0 is the water surface. If σ = 4 S/m, then the average power density is</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/62a3260ef3ff37a08d36c71442dc4bc0b884eff0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/91832dbfa7bc829a45124beb62d5d03d9fffb116.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c09fae5d04ea86d93afb7792e086ae46c987edf4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5bc943363d76955fa2588d5e78a8a0498f7681b1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1519d1531b30c95134e9a443ea01197c272902b4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/afaa539cf8f93f2d461189d82dcb9d6a94de1b71.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The wave impedance of a waveguide operating in TE mode at frequencies below cutoff frequencies is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> complex</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> purely reactive (capacitive)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> purely reactive (inductive)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> purely resistive</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f4e8e137b0a16967aa425bcd94b5c4ca4384465b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If a plane wave of 1.5 MHz progating in a medium has intrinsic impedance <img src=\"/media/fd1ca3f23cac1e35eeb3b866a608ea08d5912301.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Ω and skin depth is 2.5 m, then the conductivity of the medium is _________ × 10<sup>–2</sup> S/m.<br />\n(Rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.09","high":"2.09"},"solution":"<p>2.09 (2.00 - 2.20)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/710e5c9fbb5f960eaae594daaa8467f4bd902960.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A TE<sub>10</sub> wave at 12 GHz propagates in a dielectric (∈<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 1.44, μr = 1) filled rectangular waveguide with inner dimensions a = 1.2 cm and b = 0.6 cm. Then the wave impedance <img src=\"/media/fd5823ab4d83d4e1457691103acb995f7f64d2aa.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is _______ Ω. (Rounded off to one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"629.7","high":"629.7"},"solution":"<p>629.7 (620.0 - 635.0)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dd0c089db8213ed48f2214f63cb7210feb2293ed.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subjec